\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Coherent-oracle search for family $\mathcal  {E}$, drawn for the four-bit benchmark ($s=1010$, representative bit $b=0$, so $x_b=x_0$). (a) All registers start in $\mathinner {|{0}\rangle }$: $x$ and $y$ with $n$ qubits each, $\mathit  {cf}$ with one, and $w$ with $n-2$. State preparation applies $H$ to every input qubit except $x_b$, so the register holds the $2^{n-1}$ canonical representatives. $R$ rounds of the oracle and diffusion follow, and $x$ is measured once at the end, giving $x^{*}$. (b) The oracle computes $f$ into $y$, flips the sign of outputs in $\mathcal  {M}$, and computes $f$ again to clear $y$ (the work register $w$ serves the decompositions). (c) Detection of the canonical pattern $a=0011$. The first $X$ gates write the default $\delta =1111$ (wires $y_2,y_3$ omitted). The $X$ gate on $x_1$ selects the zero of $a$, and the multi-controlled $X$ raises $\mathit  {cf}$. CNOTs then add $\delta \oplus o=1100$ to $y$, and the detection repeats to clear $\mathit  {cf}$. The bit $x_b$ is never a control. (d) Diffusion acts on the $n-1$ search qubits only. No measurement occurs before the final readout.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:circuit}{{1}{5}{Coherent-oracle search for family $\famE $, drawn for the four-bit benchmark ($s=1010$, representative bit $b=0$, so $x_b=x_0$). (a) All registers start in $\ket {0}$: $x$ and $y$ with $n$ qubits each, $\mathit {cf}$ with one, and $w$ with $n-2$. State preparation applies $H$ to every input qubit except $x_b$, so the register holds the $2^{n-1}$ canonical representatives. $R$ rounds of the oracle and diffusion follow, and $x$ is measured once at the end, giving $x^{*}$. (b) The oracle computes $f$ into $y$, flips the sign of outputs in $\mathcal {M}$, and computes $f$ again to clear $y$ (the work register $w$ serves the decompositions). (c) Detection of the canonical pattern $a=0011$. The first $X$ gates write the default $\delta =1111$ (wires $y_2,y_3$ omitted). The $X$ gate on $x_1$ selects the zero of $a$, and the multi-controlled $X$ raises $\mathit {cf}$. CNOTs then add $\delta \oplus o=1100$ to $y$, and the detection repeats to clear $\mathit {cf}$. The bit $x_b$ is never a control. (d) Diffusion acts on the $n-1$ search qubits only. No measurement occurs before the final readout}{figure.1}{}}
